{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444865-mortal-prefects-and-governors","id":1444865,"title":"Mortal prefects and governors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-20T10:53:27-07:00","id":1444865,"title":"Mortal prefects and governors","content":"<b>What Fire Has Wrought</b> (p. 89) seems to imply that prefects and governors are Dragon-Blooded, while <b>The Realm</b> (pp. 33-34) seems to say that most prefects and all governors are mortal.<br /> <br /> 1) What is your take on this? Mortal or Dragon-Blooded prefects and governors?<br /> <br /> 2) Aren't mortal prefects, governors, and other high-ranking functionaries terribly vulnerable to the Dragon-Blooded around them? For example, Pangu is overseen by a non-Cynis prefect, something that the texts expects will change when the contract expires in two years, because Houses typically want to consolidate power in their ancestral homes (<b>The Realm</b>, p. 35). Holding on to a position of political power in a region full of Dragon-Blooded who want said power and who have Charms both social and martial seems a challenging prospect for any mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:09:48-07:00","id":1444889,"title":"","content":"Probably something like 'Her Redness appointed mortals to the positions as part of her complicated system of checks and balances and the dragon blooded could only mess with them in the most subtle of manners without ticking her off (but also meaning the mortals needed to stay in her good graces for protection). Now that she is gone so is that protection and the houses are scrambling to replace them as part of their political schemes to grab power in the vacuum of her disappearance and an increasingly large number of the posts are held by dragon blooded'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 04-20-2021, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T16:21:28-07:00","id":1445154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444865-mortal-prefects-and-governors#post1444865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What Fire Has Wrought</b> (p. 89) seems to imply that prefects and governors are Dragon-Blooded</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have that impression, but I know I would have been reading the book through a lens of already assuming that it's necessary for those bureaucrats to be mortal. Could you tell me some of the things that read like that to yourself?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Aren't mortal prefects, governors, and other high-ranking functionaries terribly vulnerable to the Dragon-Blooded around them? For example, Pangu is overseen by a non-Cynis prefect, something that the texts expects will change when the contract expires in two years, because Houses typically want to consolidate power in their ancestral homes (<b>The Realm</b>, p. 35). Holding on to a position of political power in a region full of Dragon-Blooded who want said power and who have Charms both social and martial seems a challenging prospect for any mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>For one thing, I think in many prefectures the proportion of prefect to Dragon Blood is not... overwhelming. For another, policing that kind of thing seems to be part of what the Magistrates are for. Not to mention that the competition between Dynasts means that there are going to be cases where some of them are on the side of the appointee of the Empress whose policies reflect their interests.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Social Charms, well, this Edition more than any ever emphasises the hurdles that can take place towards even magic inclining a person too far away from their self-interests or ideals that they hold to, and Dragon Blooded are not on the strongest side to that. Also, it would make sense of procedures limit the degree to which even Dynasts can actually access the person of the prefect without going through proper channels (or at least inviting them to some function that will cost you money). And as far as martial ability goes, I think that is aided much as it has been throughout real life history; that the best defence against a political scene defined by pervasive violence is to just kind of normalise that not being the default. Like, I had a conversation recently where somebody imagined the possibility of a British person embarrassing to the British government would be targeted for assassination, and it's like... that's not part of the political culture of that country the way it is for your Russia or Saudia Arabia.<br /> <br /> Of course violence in the political sphere is the norm in the Realm under the Empress <i>more</i> than it is in modern day UK, but I also kind of read it as somewhat less than it has been in much of Creation. Sure the presentation of the Realm depends on the idea that there have been underlying tensions that mean with the removal of a major stabilising factor, those norms teeter on the edge of a cliff, but still the idea that they were there.<br /> <br /> Above all else, it's just far less work to assume that it has not been necessary to constantly live with extremely beefed up security just for society and the state to function, and I don't think it even constitutes much suspension of disbelief (although that wouldn't go amiss).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444865-mortal-prefects-and-governors?p=1444889#post1444889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that she is gone so is that protection and the houses are scrambling to replace them as part of their political schemes to grab power in the vacuum of her disappearance and an increasingly large number of the posts are held by dragon blooded'</div> </div> </div> </div>My assumption is that Dynasts often don't want to be prefects, because it is a position that is... not very fun. You're doing the mundane administrative work of keeping the prefecture functional, there's not really profit or glory in it, and it's not even just the resident Dynasts who are going to be constantly inundating you with their complaints and petitions. I actually kind of recall descriptions of the few occasions on which a Dragon Blooded who doesn't from from a low status background being given the position suggesting that it's a kind of punishment. The political environment of the Realm in Year Zero is one where Houses want to control the appointments sure, but the kind of work it entails in the day to day... that's literally what the patricians are for. You appoint a patrician who is loyal to you (and that your biases surely don't bias you to the prospect that they might influence you from a disadvantaged position that nevertheless affords some power to tip the scales).<br /> <br /> Influence who the prefect is, what they do, sure, but actually being one is beneath you. It's not like being a satrap where you get to lord it over impressively furnished and exotic foreign dignitaries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-21-2021, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T18:43:58-07:00","id":1445173,"title":"","content":"What 'What Fire Has Wrought' states is that many graduates of the Spiral Academy go on to become governors, prefects, and satraps. It does not imply that they are the only ones who do so. Nor that this is the only career path they may take.<br /> <br /> There are other secondary schools beyond the main four. <br /> <br /> There are even unexalted dynasts who attend the main four --they are just held to the same academic standard as exalts-- which means that the few such who graduate from there will not be trivial opponent's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T00:06:36-07:00","id":1445234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444865-mortal-prefects-and-governors?p=1445154#post1445154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have that impression, but I know I would have been reading the book through a lens of already assuming that it's necessary for those bureaucrats to be mortal. Could you tell me some of the things that read like that to yourself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Many students believe they\u2019re being trained to push paper and nothing more, and a few in every graduating year find themselves doing that, but<b> most graduates from this august institution find themselves moving</b> not into the ministries of the Thousand Scales, but <b>into satrapial governance, prefectural and gubernatorial posts</b>, or administrative roles within their houses. </div> </div> </div>This is from <b>What Fire Has Wrought</b>, page 89, emphasis added.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444865-mortal-prefects-and-governors?p=1445154#post1445154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My assumption is that Dynasts often don't want to be prefects, because it is a position that is... not very fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sure that is true for Exalted Dynasts, but how about mortal ones?<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of the Great Houses\u2019 home prefectures \u2014 their ancestral seats of power, where their interests are strongest \u2014 are currently overseen by prefects from those houses. Dejis Prefecture boasts a Mnemon prefect; Tepet, though weakened by recent reverses, still rules Lord\u2019s Crossing; Arjuf is dominated by Ledaal. The Empress generously permitted such dominance, only occasionally \u201csuggesting\u201d a prefect from a rival house every few decades. Currently, only Cynis and Sesus have prefects from other houses in their homeprefectures, though that\u2019s likely to be remedied within the next two years. </div> </div> </div>This is from <b>The Realm</b>, page 35.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444865-mortal-prefects-and-governors?p=1445173#post1445173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What 'What Fire Has Wrought' states is that many graduates of the Spiral Academy go on to become governors, prefects, and satraps. It does not imply that they are the only ones who do so. Nor that this is the only career path they may take.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I guess all governors being mortal and many Spiral Academy graduates becoming, <i>among other things, </i>governors can technically be true at once given that a minority of Spiral Academy students are mortal.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444865-mortal-prefects-and-governors?p=1445173#post1445173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are other secondary schools beyond the main four.<br /> <br /> There are even unexalted dynasts who attend the main four --they are just held to the same academic standard as exalts-- which means that the few such who graduate from there will not be trivial opponent's.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe anyone said otherwise.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:55:30-07:00","id":1445377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444865-mortal-prefects-and-governors?p=1445234#post1445234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is from <b>What Fire Has Wrought</b>, page 89, emphasis added.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect that my reading would have been that when those are all placed in a list together, the satrapy and House administrative stuff carries a lot more weight than the prefectural postings. There isn't zero prestige to them, so they do rank among the prospects for a Dynast with administrative training, but there are higher things on the list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sure that is true for Exalted Dynasts, but how about mortal ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>{I expect they're <i>more</i> inclined towards serving as prefects and governors, but the equivalent to the private sector still offers a lot of prospects. As the books say, even the unExalted have been brought up with the kind of education determined for the Dragon Blooded, and that's a skill set the House can make much use of. You'll rank lower in the households and businesses of your Chosen cousins, but that still puts you far above all others in the Realm.}<br /> <br /> [Written halfway through the bottom paragraph]I had forgotten that The Realm says that prefects are typically the unExalted, which... I'm tired. It's perfectly cromulent for how the Blessed Isle works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is from <b>The Realm</b>, page 35.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but that's only six prefectures and two Dominions. It's a very small sample size.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlanders</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. I guess all governors being mortal and many Spiral Academy graduates becoming, <i>among other things, </i>governors can technically be true at once given that a minority of Spiral Academy students are mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it needs to be true because only a minority of governors can necessarily come from the Spiral Academy at all. I think the statement &quot;most graduates go on to such and such postings&quot; needs to consider that the Spiral Academy might well put out only fifty per year. There are hundreds of prefectures, and each can have at least a dozen governors, filling those with Exalted would be a strain on their numbers.<br /> <br /> [After revision above] With such few numbers of graduates in the first place, I would find it to be consistent that they produce maybe five or ten who can work towards the appointments that are worth the time of the Dragon Blooded. The very most lucrative or strategically important prefectures and being governors of the most glamorous cities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T23:24:31-07:00","id":1445435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444865-mortal-prefects-and-governors?p=1445377#post1445377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are hundreds of prefectures, and each can have at least a dozen governors</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here is probably the root or my confusion.<br /> <br /> I guess maybe I went into this with a second edition mindset, thinking that the places named are the only places existing.<br /> <br /> I concede that with the numbers you suggest (and which I have no reason to doubt), everything I have said is kind deflated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T02:30:20-07:00","id":1445453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444865-mortal-prefects-and-governors?p=1445435#post1445435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This right here is probably the root or my confusion.<br /> <br /> I guess maybe I went into this with a second edition mindset, thinking that the places named are the only places existing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I actually have seen fan-made maps that drew boundary lines on the Blessed Isle which acted as though the named prefectures were the only ones that existed.<br /> <br /> They overlooked how not only did the Second Edition core maintain the dimensions given in each Edition (one city, up to a dozen towns and dependent villages), they actually put a number to that figure, with a statement that they average to 100 square miles.<br /> <br /> The length and breadth of the Blessed Isle affords a lot of room for hundred mile-sided squares.<br /> <br /> I've often compared prefectures to counties of China, of which there are currently well over a thousand, even accounting for the fact that the low pop western ones are very large. And China has less land than the Blessed Isle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}